===== docs/plans/261007-csat-rating/plan.md =====
# Plan: customer satisfaction rating

Spec: `docs/specs/csat-rating.md` (approved, Mai Do, 2026-01-12). Written 2026-10-07 while the owner was away. Nothing is built; every decision below is my recommendation, to be confirmed on return.
Execution: inline, checkpoint after each phase (subagent-driven also works; phases are independent after phase 1).
Tests: `node --test` (Node 20, no dependencies). Baseline before any change: run it and paste the count.

## Phases

| # | Phase | Class | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | [Rename `assignee_id` to `owner_id`, export keeps an alias](phase-01-rename-owner.md) | COUNCIL point (export contract, production column) | not started |
| 2 | [Customer rates a resolved ticket, low score emails the owner](phase-02-rate-ticket.md) | COUNCIL point (tenant scoping, one-time write) | not started |
| 3 | [Nightly weekly summary per agent](phase-03-weekly-summary.md) | ACT | not started |
| 4 | [Docs, independent review, finance notice](phase-04-close-out.md) | ACT | not started |

Phase 1 goes first so phases 2 and 3 write `owner_id` once and are never renamed afterwards.

## Requirement coverage

| Spec requirement | Phase |
|---|---|
| 1 rate 1 to 5 from the portal | 2 |
| 2 at most one rating | 2 |
| 3 own organisation only | 2 |
| 4 score 1 or 2 emails the agent | 2 |
| 5 nightly weekly summary | 3 |
| 6 rename to `owner_id` | 1 |

## Files

Modify: `src/tickets.js`, `src/store.js`, `src/portal.js`, `src/jobs/export-tickets.js`, `docs/glossary.md`, `README.md`, `test/tickets.test.js`, `test/export-tickets.test.js`.
Create: `src/jobs/rating-summary.js`, `test/rating.test.js`, `test/rating-summary.test.js`.

## Validation questions and recommended answers

Answers are my recommendations; the plan is built on them.

**Q1. The export is read by finance's job, which finance deploys on its own schedule. A bare rename breaks it. What do we do?**
A: The export carries both `owner_id` and `assignee_id` (same value). Everything else in the repo says only `owner_id`. The alias is marked in code and removed when finance confirms. You must tell finance; that cannot be done from here. Spec criterion "called `owner_id` wherever it was `assignee_id`" is met for all storage and code, with this one declared exception.

**Q2. Which tickets can be rated?**
A: Resolved only, as the spec says. A resolved ticket closes after 3 quiet days (`src/jobs/close-resolved.js:5`), so a customer has about three days. Mai should know the window is that short. A ticket that was rated and then reopened keeps its rating and cannot be rated again.

**Q3. Where is the rating stored?**
A: On the ticket row as `rating` and `rated_at` ("stored with the ticket"). It survives the purge job, which deletes messages and keeps the row (`src/jobs/purge-closed.js:15`).

**Q4. How are refusals reported?**
A: As the portal already does: a ticket of another organisation or a missing one returns `null` (same answer, checked before anything else so the score or status never leaks); a bad score, wrong status or second rating throws an `Error`.

**Q5. Score 1 or 2 on a ticket nobody owns?**
A: Rating succeeds, no email is queued, nothing throws (`notifyAgent` throws without an agent, `src/notify.js:7`).

**Q6. Where does the weekly summary go and what shape?**
A: `exports/agent-ratings.json`, a separate file from the finance export: `{ generated_at, since, agents: [{ agent_id, ratings, average }] }`, average rounded to 2 decimals, sorted by `agent_id`, agents with no ratings left out. "Past seven days" means `rated_at` from `now - 7 days` up to `now`, both inclusive.

**Q7. Which agent gets a rating in the summary?**
A: The ticket's current `owner_id` when the job runs. The code keeps no ownership history.

**Q8. The production database?**
A: The Postgres store lives outside this repo. It needs `rating`, `rated_at`, and the `assignee_id` to `owner_id` column change. Recommended as expand then contract: add `owner_id`, write both, backfill, switch readers, drop `assignee_id` later. That migration is a separate COUNCIL change, not in this plan. Phase 2 also needs the store's `rateTicket` to be one conditional `UPDATE ... WHERE status = 'resolved' AND rating IS NULL`.

## Out of scope

Renaming `assignTicket`; showing ratings to agents in the back office; rating closed tickets; changing the 3-day close rule.
